  "source_excerpts": {
    "title": "Commutator-certified border reduction of sparse decomposition algebras",
    "mechanism": "Object: a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps. Operation set Sigma: extend the border, reduce products, and close commutator defects. Trichotomy: coordinate-dependent; this is a solver/representation object, not a lossy quotient under the full group translation action. Discarded information: polynomials are represented by quotient classes, discarding ideal multiples; completeness needs both containment directions and a certified quotient dimension. Construct candidate border bases for the actual finite decomposition ideal using an adaptive support budget, retaining reduction witnesses from original generators. Close every multiplication commutator and verify generator annihilation. A small staircase supplied by interpolation from known solutions is forbidden as a free input; its discovery cost and all failed candidates are charged.",
    "minimal_test": {
      "design": "p of 12,16,20 bits, m=2,3, s=3..5; three curves and matched SAT/UNSAT targets. Check exact quotient dimension by independent exhaustive enumeration at the smallest cells.",
      "execution_status": "design_only_not_approved",
      "controls": [
        {
          "kind": "baseline",
          "design": "Fix the staircase to the grevlex normal set and its canonical reductions; reproduce the ordinary quotient multiplication representation."
        },
        {
          "kind": "matched_null",
          "design": "Same support/zero-count polynomial systems and a matched random staircase schedule."
        },
        {
          "kind": "known_false",
          "design": "Matrices annihilating the supplied generators but not commuting must fail; commuting maps with the wrong quotient dimension must not certify completeness."
        },
        {
          "kind": "identity",
          "design": "Use the stated baseline slice with identical inputs, ordering and certificate policy; output identities must match exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "generic_group",
          "design": "For any claimed group information gain, repeat the statistic on relabelled Z/NZ with the same incidence and acquisition budget. Algebra-only comparisons explicitly do not claim a generic-group escape."
        }
      ],
      "required_metrics": [
        "nonzeros in multiplication matrices, candidate attempts, commutator closure cost, total field operations",
        "all setup, acquisition, unsuccessful-attempt, transport, certificate and verification costs",
        "peak resident memory and total stored bytes",
        "SAT and UNSAT costs separately, or successful and failed incidence attempts separately",
        "loss L=log2(number of represented preimages) and branching b=max verified successors at each retained synopsis; witness storage separately"
      ],
      "budget": {
        "proposed_only": true,
        "maximum_runs": 0,
        "note": "This handoff approves zero runs. A successor needs a new frozen per-cell budget; planning allowance 3 implementation-days and up to 4 CPU-hours/32 GiB for first complete toy cell, scaled only by Coordinator approval. Exhaustive synthetic calibrators may warrant smaller documented bounds."
      },
      "stopping_rules": [
        "Stop on first soundness/completeness control failure and classify the instrument invalid.",
        "At a frozen resource cap report failed_infrastructure without a mathematical verdict.",
        "If valid completed cells miss the quantitative threshold, reject only this mechanism/parameter claim and retain the measured obstruction."
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "frozen source formula/curve/base and seeds",
        "all candidate descriptions and failed attempts",
        "exact control and solution certificates",
        "stage-cost and memory records",
        "independent checker source binding",
        "unpooled raw metrics"
      ]
    },
    "falsification_conditions": [
      "Any valid completed cell exhibits the known-false failure: Matrices annihilating the supplied generators but not commuting must fail; commuting maps with the wrong quotient dimension must not certify completeness.",
      "The completed controlled ladder fails the proposed effect: Total construction+verification+recovery <=0.5 F4, with identical quotient dimension and roots",
      "The charged saving disappears after including construction, canonicalization, failed attempts, memory or recovery.",
      "A purported synopsis merges the collision pair without retaining its distinction: Equal quotient dimensions but nonisomorphic multiplication tables demonstrate why dimension alone cannot certify the ideal."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Public generated mathematical instances only, with frozen field, subgroup, curve, factor-base definition, presentation, solver and sample law.",
      "F2 factor-base decomposition is a component, not the proposed new object; the added object is a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps. F1 generic search is a comparator; any F7 caching/preprocessing is fully charged.",
      "All identity, soundness and completeness certificates must be independently checked before measuring cost.",
      "Prime-field digit/implicit membership is a high-degree or implicit-description escape class of KN-OPEN-020, not a bounded-degree plane-locus exemption. Binary arms use actual Weil descent and never transfer Boolean identities to F_p."
    ],
    "proof_search_map": {
      "bottleneck": "The exact load-bearing step is producing and using a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps cheaply enough for: Total construction+verification+recovery <=0.5 F4, with identical quotient dimension and roots",
      "baseline_embedding": {
        "parameter_slice": "Fix the staircase to the grevlex normal set and its canonical reductions; reproduce the ordinary quotient multiplication representation.",
        "reproduction_check": "First prove this equality symbolically; in a successor compare every output/certificate at the smallest exhaustive fixture. No reproduction was executed in this task."
      },
      "observation_collision": {
        "observable": "a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps",
        "distinct_preimage_search": "Equal quotient dimensions but nonisomorphic multiplication tables demonstrate why dimension alone cannot certify the ideal."
      },
      "constructive_transforms": [
        {
          "transform": "representation_reduction",
          "proposed_object": "a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps",
          "predicted_gain": "Total construction+verification+recovery <=0.5 F4, with identical quotient dimension and roots"
        }
      ],
      "quantifier_order": "For every admitted public instance in the frozen parameter family, construct certificates with soundness and completeness; for the preregistered distribution and selected fixed design, H1 predicts Total construction+verification+recovery <=0.5 F4, with identical quotient dimension and roots. Selection may depend on public parameters and charged calibration, never on hidden scalar labels or evaluation outcomes.",
      "method_ceiling": {
        "strongest_certifiable_claim": "A sparse connected staircase may reduce multiplication/reduction work by at least 2x relative to grevlex F4 on the identical prime-field digit system while preserving exact solutions. It need not reduce the mathematical solving-degree invariant. A successful finite test is scoped evidence only; a uniform asymptotic theorem requires a separate bound on every growth parameter.",
        "nearby_object_control": "Matrices annihilating the supplied generators but not commuting must fail; commuting maps with the wrong quotient dimension must not certify completeness."
      },
      "proof_obligations": [
        {
          "responsibility": "baseline",
          "claim": "Fix the staircase to the grevlex normal set and its canonical reductions; reproduce the ordinary quotient multiplication representation."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "correctness",
          "claim": "Prove that extend the border, reduce products, and close commutator defects preserves precisely the asserted solution/row/certificate property, with exact witnesses."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "interface",
          "claim": "Prove recovery after the declared loss: polynomials are represented by quotient classes, discarding ideal multiples; completeness needs both containment directions and a certified quotient dimension; independently verify every final group relation."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "size",
          "claim": "Bound all retained data for a connected monomial order ideal with exact commuting quotient multiplication maps including nonzeros in multiplication matrices, candidate attempts, commutator closure cost, total field operations and certificate storage."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "runtime",
          "claim": "Derive and charge the entire expression: Sum all candidate construction costs+C_commute+C_containment+C_recovery; M=all retained multiplication nonzeros plus proof witnesses; data=original generators, candidate schedule and failed candidates."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "success_probability",
          "claim": "The exact quotient has a connected staircase discovered within <=4 candidates with <=half the multiplication nonzeros of grevlex; verification overhead stays below saved reduction work. Establish or test this separately from runtime and correctness."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "strictness",
          "claim": "Exhibit completed controlled evidence or a theorem for Total construction+verification+recovery <=0.5 F4, with identical quotient dimension and roots; equal solution count or low output degree alone does not establish it."
        }
      ],
      "not_applicable_reason": null
    },
    "interpretation_limits": [
      "Proposals only: no experiment, proof validation, asymptotic improvement, verified novelty, hypothesis transition or goal completion.",
      "All cost inequalities are targets or conditional algebraic accounting, not measurements. Matched Pollard rho O(N^(1/2)) group operations, small memory; BSGS O(N^(1/2)) time and memory. These generic reference rows do not establish that the proposed method wins.",
      "R3 labels the attacked representation stage, not a new group law. Loss or branching must be certified against Sigma; no full-translation quotient claim.",
      "Degree, reduced-basis size, rank deficit, first fall and actual solving work are distinct. The known shared S_4 defect record must be audited before reusing any old implementation.",
      "Negative evidence would concern the exact tested representation, operations, domain and budget-independent completed cells only."
    ],
